# phi-agent — directories the coding agent (A2) and the A1 folder-of-interest
# picker must refuse (phios-agente-delta.md §3.4).
#
# Copy to ~/.config/phi-agent/code-blocklist and edit. One glob per line;
# '#' starts a comment; '~' expands to $HOME. A path that equals or is inside
# a listed pattern is refused, with `phi agent code` (or the folder picker)
# printing one line and starting nothing.
#
# This is a GUARD-RAIL on the picker, never the security boundary. The
# boundary is phi-agent-contain's from-empty mount namespace: even a path
# that slips past this list is still the ONLY directory the session sees.
#
# The always-denied set (never listed here, cannot be removed): ~/.ssh,
# ~/.gnupg, the password store, ~/.config/phi-agent, keyrings, /etc, and —
# for the A2 read-write mount — /usr /var /opt /srv /nix, $HOME itself, /.
#
# Also editable from Settings › AI Agent.

# Your dotfiles and phiOS repositories — let A2 work on a checkout you made,
# not on the live tree the installer applies.
~/phios-dotfiles
~/phi
~/phi-shell
~/phi-packages

# The synced cloud root (ADR 045) — notes and documents, not code.
~/cloud

# System configuration you keep under version control elsewhere.
~/.config/nvim
~/.local/share/phi
